{"author":{"id":"2f242a7e7f2592f8909954a77fabece74f6e8cc197182647ed3b15ea8e3878af"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791139594,"nonce":"qhrwfhEEB6eXJQPxWb+YRkhRJEs=","title":"dragWindow on macOS makes a borderless window jump","message":"Reported by ashui-8b. winit's drag_window calls performWindowDragWithEvent: with NSApp.currentEvent. xwindow hands events to the program after the pump returns, so when a pointer-down handler calls dragWindow the current event is no longer that mouse-down, and AppKit drags from the wrong origin.\n\nProposed fix: keep the last left mouse-down NSEvent (the local event monitor added for polls, widened to left mouse-down, can see it), and on macOS have window_drag call performWindowDragWithEvent: with it rather than through winit.\n\nashui works around it with setPosition. Native dragging matters for edge snapping, moving between Spaces, and Wayland, where it is the only way.","files":null}]}